        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "the feverish pride of a controversialist is inexhaustible; those",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "who are filled with wealth serve you; even me serve those",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "that have a longing to listen to me that the taint of their",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "hearts may be removed; if you have no respect for me, the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "less have I for you; O king, here am I off.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "54. Here we are satisfied with barks, and you with silk",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "garments; the satisfaction is equal in this case and the dis-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "tinction is without difference. Let him be ( called ) poor",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "whose greed is boundless; the heart being content who is",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "rich and who is poor ?",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "55. Fruits for a meal, sweet water for drink, the (bare)",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "surface of the earth for a bed, and barks for raimnent, are",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "all good (preferable) enough; but I cannot tolerate ( lit.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "sanction ) the impudence of wicked men, all whose senses",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "have been maddened by the fresh ( acquisition of ) wealth as",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "if by drinking wine.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "56. We live on alms, cover ourselves with the directions",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "serving as garments, and lie down on the surface of the earth:",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "what have we to do with big folks ?",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "57. Of what value, indeed, are we in a royal palace since",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "we are neither actors, nor flatterers, nor singers; nor have",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "we our hearts set on hating others; nor are we ( beautiful )",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "women bent down with the burden of the breasts ?",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r7",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "58. The world was formerly created by certain large-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "hearted blessed persons; by some it was sustained, and by",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "others it was conquered and given away as if it were grass;",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "other noble persons even now rule the fourteen worlds.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "What morbid infatuation is it on the part of men when they",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "have acquired rulership over a few towns ?",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r8",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "59. What honour is it to kings to obtain ( the rulership",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "of ) the earth, which was not left unenjoyed even for a mo-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "ment by hundreds of kings; but the lords of a part of its",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "( earth's ) part, and of even a small part of that part—fools",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
